1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,154
I returned the money at dawn because a
tree branch frightened me. Lucia

2
00:00:05,154 --> 00:00:06,740
won't let me forget.

3
00:00:06,740 --> 00:00:11,897
Hours earlier, three cracks hit the
rental shed. I killed the lamp and

4
00:00:11,897 --> 00:00:13,880
crouched beside our stolen duffel.

5
00:00:13,880 --> 00:00:19,028
I wanted the back door. Lucia held my
sleeve. Three cracks repeated, in

6
00:00:19,028 --> 00:00:19,820
identical rhythm.

7
00:00:19,820 --> 00:00:24,972
She pointed up. Wind bent a rotten
branch against a loose shutter. I

8
00:00:24,972 --> 00:00:27,350
laughed before I could stop myself.

9
00:00:27,350 --> 00:00:32,108
Then a flashlight crossed the yard. An
anonymous caretaker walked past us,

10
00:00:32,108 --> 00:00:34,090
close enough to hear us.

11
00:00:34,090 --> 00:00:39,249
He secured the branch and left. We
stayed frozen beside the kayaks until

12
00:00:39,249 --> 00:00:40,440
his light vanished.

13
00:00:40,440 --> 00:00:45,592
Lucia switched the lamp on. The cash was
still there. I couldn't remember

14
00:00:45,592 --> 00:00:47,970
what it was supposed to fix.

15
00:00:47,970 --> 00:00:53,887
At dawn, we left it for its owner. The
branch hadn't threatened my life.

16
00:00:53,887 --> 00:00:56,000
It had shown me mine.
